*  \nI prefer **d7-d5** because it immediately fights for the center, prevents White from playing e4 easily (since Nf3 alone doesn’t fully support it), and opens the diagonal for the c8 bishop. It also keeps options open for both knights’ development next move (Nc6 or Nf6). Other moves like e7-e5 would allow White to push d4 quickly, gaining more central space; d7-d5 avoids that early. Nf6 is also fine, but it’s less direct in center battle on move 1.\n\n**Answer:** P: d7-d5'}
